    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0199" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg107"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bridgman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                                Paz, Bolivia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I received
                    on April 17 the following cablegram from the Department: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>On request British Government you will protect British subjects and
                            interests if necessary. Notify Bolivian authorities.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0200" n="108" xml:id="pg108"/>
                <p>I will notify the Bolivian Government of the same as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>At present there is no need of protection, as everything is quiet. I have in
                    several instances protected British interests in the absence of any English
                    representative.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George H.
                    Bridgman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
